 a rigid kind of ideology  that i think reflects uh very poorly on  the united states it sends a terrible  signal to other allies around the world  it sends a terrible signal to the  government of colombia for example  which is criticized by some on the left  in this country for  abuses by civil militias that are  opposing the  narco terrorists who run much of the  country even though those narco  terrorists are in league with hugo  chavez being supplied by weapons their  funding comes from the  sale of illegal drugs you know when you  kick around  a tiny country like honduras uh  in the way that we have i i i think it  again leads people to say  that uh that you have to be careful of  having a friend in washington  and in the back there  yeah my name is bruce kaufman um you  spoke early about  the obama administration at some point  hoping to get back under the  jurisdiction of the international  criminal court  and that there might be some criticism  that wouldn't one of the criticisms to  the extent that that would put  american citizens under the jurisdiction  of an international court  wouldn't one of the criticisms be that  it's unconstitutional  and second thing is this another example  of post-america  well i i think that it i think is an  example of post-americanism and i think  it's part of a long  series of efforts by by  people who style themselves as advocates  of international human rights to try and  constrain the united states  you know we we have the best program  in the world bar none for training  people in our military to obey the laws  of war  we have  considerable enforcement capability when  our soldiers  for for unacceptable reasons violate  our laws their training and our doctrine  we don't hesitate to enforce these  prohibitions  we have i would be happy to hold up the  american record against  any other country in the world it is  true that sometimes  our soldiers do commit  crimes that violate our laws a little  secret here  our country i